POSITION DESCRIPTION


TITLE:                                Help Desk Engineer (Level 3 Support)
CLASSIFICATION:                Administrative/Technical
DEPARTMENT:                Information Technology
FLSA STATUS:                Exempt
SYSTEM JOB TITLE:                 Senior Technical Engineer
SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Assistant Chief Information Officer for Client Success
SUPERVISION EXERCISED:  User Support Analysts, Student Technicians
POSITION SUMMARY: The Help Desk Engineer serves as a senior-level technical resource with expert-level knowledge of Apple and Windows Operating Systems, enterprise infrastructure, and complex IT environments. This role provides Level 3 escalated support, leads technical projects, architects solutions for campus-wide technology deployments, and serves as a technical mentor to support staff. Acts as the primary technical liaison between end-user support and infrastructure teams while maintaining a customer-focused approach to complex technical challenges.


ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES:

ADVANCED TECHNICAL SUPPORT & ESCALATIONS:
* Serve as the final escalation point for complex Level 3 technical issues that cannot be resolved by Level 1/2 support staff
* Diagnose and resolve advanced system, network, application, and infrastructure problems requiring deep technical expertise
* Perform root cause analysis on recurring technical issues and implement permanent solutions
* Lead critical incident response and coordinate resolution efforts across multiple IT teams
* Provide expert-level support for Moravian-issued devices including advanced troubleshooting of desktops, laptops, tablets, mobile devices, and peripherals across iOS/iPadOS, MacOS, and Windows environments

FLEET MANAGEMENT & ENDPOINT SYSTEMS:
* Assist with JAMF Pro MDM administration for Apple device management, deployment, and policy configuration
* Support Kace systems management platform operations including imaging, patching, and software deployment
* Maintain and optimize endpoint device configurations, software packages, and deployment workflows
* Support enterprise endpoint protection, encryption, and security solutions on managed devices
* Collaborate with systems team on Active Directory, Group Policy, and Microsoft 365 configurations as they relate to endpoint management
* Assist with Google Workspace for Education support related to device and user access issues
* Provide Level 2/3 support for Jenzabar EX administrative software, AMOS/JICS, and other enterprise applications from an end-user perspective
* Troubleshoot device connectivity issues and coordinate with Network Services team for infrastructure-related problems

PROJECT MANAGEMENT & IMPLEMENTATION:
* Lead technology deployment projects from planning through implementation and documentation
* Design and implement automated deployment solutions for hardware and software
* Develop and execute mass deployment strategies for operating system upgrades and software rollouts
* Create and maintain system images, deployment packages, and configuration profiles
* Evaluate new technologies and make recommendations for enterprise adoption
* Plan and execute technology refresh cycles for faculty, staff, and institutional equipment

TECHNICAL LEADERSHIP & MENTORSHIP:
* Provide technical guidance and mentorship to User Support Analysts and Help Desk staff
* Develop and deliver advanced technical training for IT team members
* Create and maintain comprehensive technical documentation including procedures, knowledge base articles, and troubleshooting guides
* Establish best practices and standard operating procedures for support operations
* Lead technical review sessions and post-incident analyses
* Supervise and develop student technicians

COLLABORATION & COMMUNICATION:
* Work closely with Network Services, Systems Engineering, AV Engineering, Applications Development, Information Security, and Events Technology teams on endpoint-related issues
* Serve as primary point of contact between end-user support and infrastructure/engineering teams for device and application issues
* Escalate network, server, and infrastructure issues to appropriate teams with thorough documentation
* Participate in IT planning meetings and contribute to endpoint strategy and user experience initiatives
* Communicate complex technical concepts to non-technical audiences effectively
* Coordinate with vendors on advanced endpoint troubleshooting, warranty claims, and technical escalations including Apple GSX
* Utilize ITSM ticketing system (TDX) for comprehensive documentation, metrics tracking, and workflow management

OPERATIONAL EXCELLENCE:
* Monitor system health, performance metrics, and support trends to identify improvement opportunities
* Maintain precise inventory management and asset lifecycle tracking
* Oversee IT loaner program including hardware allocation, tracking, and maintenance
* Ensure compliance with security policies, licensing agreements, and regulatory requirements
* Participate in on-call rotation for after-hours critical incident response
* Stay current with emerging technologies through continuous learning, certifications, webinars, and professional development

ADDITIONAL RESPONSIBILITIES:
* Perform special projects and all other job-related duties as assigned
* Required to work some evenings, weekends, and holidays as needed
* Required to operate a company vehicle and travel periodically to satellite campus locations
* Level II - Essential Personnel


QUALIFICATIONS:

REQUIRED:
* Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or related field AND 5+ years of progressive IT support experience
  OR Associate's degree with 7+ years of experience
  OR 10+ years of relevant technical experience in lieu of degree
* Expert-level knowledge of Apple MacOS and Windows 10/11 operating systems
* Advanced experience with endpoint management and fleet deployment tools
* Proven experience supporting MDM solutions (JAMF Pro highly preferred)
* Strong experience with systems management platforms for endpoint support (Kace, SCCM, or similar)
* Demonstrated experience leading endpoint deployment projects and managing device lifecycles
* Advanced troubleshooting and problem-solving abilities with complex endpoint, application, and user access issues
* Excellent customer service orientation with ability to manage difficult situations professionally
* Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, including ability to document technical processes clearly
* Proven ability to work independently, prioritize competing demands, and manage multiple projects simultaneously
* Strong analytical and critical thinking skills

PREFERRED:
* Relevant technical certifications such as:
  - Apple Certified Support Professional (ACSP) or Apple Certified Technical Coordinator (ACTC)
  - Apple GSX certification
  - Microsoft Certified: Modern Desktop Administrator Associate
  - JAMF Certified Tech or Certified Admin
  - CompTIA A+, Security+, or equivalent
  - ITIL Foundation or higher
* Experience in higher education IT environment
* Scripting/automation experience for endpoint management tasks (PowerShell, Bash, Python, or similar)
* Experience with Microsoft Intune or other cloud-based endpoint management platforms
* Understanding of networking fundamentals as they relate to device connectivity and troubleshooting
* Experience with backup and device recovery solutions
* Familiarity with ITSM platforms (TeamDynamix, ServiceNow, or similar)
* Experience with application packaging and deployment

TECHNICAL PROFICIENCIES:
* Advanced proficiency in MacOS, Windows 10/11, iOS/iPadOS
* Microsoft 365 end-user and device support (Exchange Online, SharePoint, Teams, OneDrive)
* JAMF Pro MDM support and Apple GSX warranty management
* Kace Systems Management Suite for endpoint support
* Understanding of Active Directory and Group Policy as they relate to endpoint configuration
* TDX or similar ITSM/ticketing systems
* Remote support tools (TeamViewer, LogMeIn, Remote Desktop, etc.)
* Device connectivity and wireless troubleshooting
* Google Workspace for Education user support
* Endpoint protection and security solutions
* Imaging and deployment technologies
* Scripting and automation for endpoint tasks (PowerShell, Bash, etc.)
* Application packaging and software deployment


